4. Deployment Reality: Kubernetes + Istio
Important truth:

O2Adaptor security and exposure is NOT handled in Java code.
It is handled at Kubernetes + Istio level.

5. Why Istio is used

Problems without Istio:

TLS logic in every service

Manual certificate handling

No mTLS

Hardcoded routing

Istio solves:

TLS / mTLS

Traffic routing

Retry / timeout

Zero-trust networking

6. Sidecar concept (CORE CONCEPT)

Every pod has two containers:

Pod
 ├── O2Adaptor Application
 └── Envoy Sidecar (Istio proxy)


Envoy sidecar handles:

TLS / mTLS

Encryption

Routing

Egress / Ingress control

Application does not know TLS exists.

7. Two-Sidecar Model (what team meant)

Whenever one service talks to another:

Caller Pod
 ├── App
 └── Sidecar  ---> encrypted traffic --->

Receiver Pod
 ├── Sidecar
 └── App


This is called two-sidecar solution.

8. Ingress vs Egress (very important)
Ingress

Traffic coming into the cluster

Example:

O-Cloud team → O2Adaptor callback URL


Handled by:

Istio Ingress Gateway

Gateway + VirtualService

Egress

Traffic going out of the cluster

Example:

O2Adaptor → O-Cloud Simulator / external API


Handled by:

Sidecar

ServiceEntry

(Optional) Egress Gateway

9. Gateway vs VirtualService (key confusion resolved)
Gateway

Defines HOW traffic enters

Port (443)

Protocol (HTTPS)

TLS on/off

Certificate

VirtualService

Defines WHERE traffic goes

URL path

Target service

Routing rules

Flow:
Request
 → Gateway (opens door)
 → VirtualService (routes)
 → O2Adaptor service


That is why team said:

“VirtualService se hoga”

Meaning:

Routing will be done by Istio config, not by application.

10. TLS & HTTPS (basic but critical)

HTTPS = HTTP + TLS

TLS encrypts traffic

Certificates are stored as Kubernetes Secrets

TLS terminates at Ingress Gateway

Inside cluster → HTTP + mTLS via sidecars

11. Exact Task Given by Lead (decoded)
Statement:

“We need to configure ingress gateway and provide the endpoint details to O-Cloud team so they can connect using the ingress gateway and http-route to the O2 Adaptor service in SMO.”

Meaning:

Expose O2Adaptor securely

Use Istio Ingress Gateway

Route traffic via VirtualService

No Spring Boot code change

Deliver HTTPS endpoint to O-Cloud team

12. Exact YAML configuration you are expected to add
12.1 Istio Ingress Gateway
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: Gateway
metadata:
  name: o2adaptor-ingress-gateway
  namespace: smo
spec:
  selector:
    istio: ingressgateway
  servers:
  - port:
      number: 443
      name: https
      protocol: HTTPS
    tls:
      mode: SIMPLE
      credentialName: o2adaptor-tls-secret
    hosts:
    - o2adaptor.smo.example.com

12.2 VirtualService
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: o2adaptor-virtualservice
  namespace: smo
spec:
  hosts:
  - o2adaptor.smo.example.com
  gateways:
  - o2adaptor-ingress-gateway
  http:
  - match:
    - uri:
        prefix: /o2ims/notification
    route:
    - destination:
        host: o2adaptor
        port:
          number: 8081

12.3 Service (already exists)
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: o2adaptor
spec:
  ports:
  - port: 8081
    targetPort: 8081

